s strategic advisory services, such as mergers, and acquisitions, strategic, defense, and shareholder advisory, special committee assignments, and real estate strategic advisory; private capital advisory and fundraising, market risk management and hedging, private capital markets and debt advisory, liability management and restructuring, and equity capital markets execution and advisory services; and research, sales, and trading professionals services on a content-led platform to its institutional investor clients. The Investment Management segment provides wealth management services to high-net-worth individuals, foundations, and endowments. The company was formerly known as Evercore Partners Inc. and changed its name to Evercore Inc. in August 2017. Evercore Inc. was founded in 1995 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John S. Weinberg | Chairman & CEO | Age 68 | Compensation: $11.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $417K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $238K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Evercore Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $10.3B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 44% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 32-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 34\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4471561.14},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 24% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range 